ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":157,"prev":159,"next":161,"titles":163,"firmware":60},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":17,"status":18,"firmware":19,"facts":27,"procedures":83,"parameters":117,"related":125,"body":129,"sources":130,"official_url":31,"controls":140},"arrange.song-mode","Song mode",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"song","song order","chain scenes","song arrangement","loop song","song editor","arrange",50,"knowledge/manual/units/arrange/song-mode.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[11],[5],"Song mode chains scenes into a song order of up to 96 slots — dialled in with shift and the black keys, edited with a cursor, and set to loop or not with `E1`.","current",{"min":20,"changed_in":21,"guide_version":25,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[22,23,24],"1.0.29","1.0.45","1.1.0","1.1.15",null,[28,33,36,40,43,46,49,52,56,62,67,71,74,77,80],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"enter","In arrange mode, `shift + arrange` opens song mode.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/arrange#song-mode","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"add","Holding `shift` and pressing black keys appends scenes to the song order one after another, much like keying in a phone number.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":39,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"shift-needed","Since OS 1.1.0, adding scenes and switching songs in song mode need `shift`.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":31,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"max","A song order holds up to 96 scenes.",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"cursor","`shift + M2` and `shift + M3` move a cursor back and forth through the song order, so scenes can be inserted between others or removed.",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"delete","`shift + M4` takes the scene at the cursor out of the song; the scene itself stays in the project.",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"clear","`shift + M1` empties the whole song order without deleting any scene.",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":55,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"stop-at-end","OS 1.0.45 added the option of stopping playback when the song reaches its end.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.45",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":59,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"plain-play","Play runs the current song from its first scene even outside song mode, and after a stop play starts it from the first scene again, unless a scene was picked in arrange first, which then plays instead.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-28-night--songs-and-scenes-on-the-unit-owner-present-tes-agent-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":65,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":66},"leave-held","While a scene is held on repeat, going into song mode does not cut it off; the song's first scene is cued for when the held scene ends its cycle, and then the song carries on through its order. Before this the held scene would have looped for ever (one video, narrated).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":68,"text":69,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"screen","The song page is headed song 1 with a loop icon and shows a grid of 32 slots, eight across in four rows marked 1, 9, 17 and 25; scenes appear as numbered circles, a white line marks where the next scene goes, and a ring walks along the order during playback.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#29-arrange-and-song-mode",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"count","The box beside count at the top right shows how many scenes the song holds.",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"cursor-with-shift","The white cursor line shows only while `shift` is held, together with the lit footer.",{"id":78,"text":79,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"ring","During playback the playing scene wears a white ring with a small notch that goes round once while the scene plays; after stop the ring stays on the scene that was playing.",{"id":81,"text":82,"source":70,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":60,"confidence":61},"footer","Holding `shift` lights the footer with clear all, ←, → and delete over `M1`…`M4`, the song editing keys.",[84,97,109],{"id":85,"goal":86,"preconditions":87,"steps":90,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"build","Build a song from scenes",[88,89],"arrange mode","the scenes exist",[91,94],{"keys":92,"note":93,"set":26},"shift + arrange","opens song mode",{"keys":95,"note":96,"set":26},"shift + accidentals","add the scenes in playing order",{"id":98,"goal":99,"preconditions":100,"steps":102,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"insert","Insert a scene between two others",[101],"song mode",[103,106],{"keys":104,"note":105,"set":26},"shift + M2/M3","move the cursor to the insertion point",{"keys":107,"note":108,"set":26},"shift + accidental","the scene to insert",{"id":47,"goal":110,"preconditions":111,"steps":112,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"Take a scene out of the song",[101],[113,115],{"keys":104,"note":114,"set":26},"move the cursor to it",{"keys":116,"note":26,"set":26},"shift + M4",[118],{"screen":5,"encoder":119,"layer":120,"keys":121,"name":122,"range":123,"default":26,"cc":26,"cc_confidence":26,"note":124,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"E1","base","turn E1","loop","off / on","when on, the song starts over from its first scene after the last one",[126,127,128],"arrange.songs","arrange.scenes","arrange.scene-queue","Song mode t